  <content>
  <section><title>Warm Up Activity</title>
<para><figure><media alt="Ticket stubs"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/4c2ff88a8ad938c925c3489dbf177ecda8d6e508"/></media></figure></para>
<para>Tickets to a play cost $12, and for each purchase there is a $2.50 fee. The expression \(12t + 2.50\) represents the cost to purchase tickets for the play, where \(t\) is the number of tickets. Be prepared to explain your response to each question.</para>

<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>A family paid $62.50 for tickets. How many tickets were bought?</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter the number of tickets.</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>Five tickets were bought. Subtracting 2.50 from 62.50 gives 60. If \(12t\) is 60, then \(t\) is 5.</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->
<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>A teacher paid $278.50 for tickets for her students. How many tickets were bought?</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter the number of tickets.</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>Twenty-three tickets were bought. Subtracting 2.50 from 278.50 gives 276. If \(12t\) is 276, then \(t\) is 23.</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End --></section>
</content>
